# ============================================================================
# deploy/.dockerignore — keep the build context tiny (MB, not GB)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud-Migration PHASE 0 — AUTHORED, UNVERIFIED (Docker absent on this machine).
#
# ACTIVATION NOTE (important): Docker reads the ignore file from the BUILD
# CONTEXT ROOT (or, under BuildKit, `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`). It does
# NOT auto-read deploy/.dockerignore. So before building, the operator must make
# this file the active one, e.g. from the repo root:
#     cp deploy/.dockerignore .dockerignore        # then: docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .
#   OR (BuildKit-native, no root file):
#     cp deploy/.dockerignore deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore
# See deploy/PHASE0_README.md for the full build recipe.
#
# GOAL: the old `COPY . .` dragged .git (3.4 GB), the prod DB (652 MB), the R&D
# DB (36 GB), docs and spreadsheets into the context. This image copies ONLY
# backend/ + scripts/ + requirements.txt, so everything else is excluded here to
# keep the context small and the build fast.
# ============================================================================

# ── Version control (3.4 GB — the 680 GiB git-bloat incident lives here) ─────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
**/.git

# ── Databases — NEVER in the serving image (mounted at runtime instead) ──────
# Prod SQLite (652 MB) is a mounted volume; the R&D warehouse (36 GB) must never
# ship. SQLite WAL/SHM sidecars excluded too.
data/
**/data/db/
universe_engine/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# ── Secrets & env — baked NOWHERE; injected at runtime ───────────────────────
config/.env
config/.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ── Python caches / build junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Docs / reports / office files (docs/ops is full of xlsx/docx) ────────────
docs/
**/*.xlsx
**/*.xlsm
**/*.docx
**/*.doc
**/*.pdf
**/*.pptx
README.md
*.md

# ── Backups & artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.bak
**/*.bak.*
**/_backups/
data/artifacts/
data/config/
*.log
logs/

# ── Sibling git worktrees (the _kanida_* trees on the operator's Desktop) ────
# These live OUTSIDE the repo so they aren't normally in-context, but guard
# anyway in case a build is ever run from a parent directory.
_kanida_*/
../_kanida_*/

# ── Frontend / node (backend image never needs these) ────────────────────────
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# ── Tests are not needed to SERVE (uncomment to shrink further; kept by default
#    so the image can self-test with pytest if desired) ────────────────────────
# backend/tests/
# **/tests/

# ── This deploy/ dir itself (compose/terraform/docs aren't app runtime) ──────
deploy/terraform/
deploy/*.md
deploy/docker-compose.yml
deploy/cloudflared
